    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Hambagu takes 35 minutes and serves four. It is a Japanese-style meat patty, softer and looser than a burger. The texture comes from a high ratio of onion, panko breadcrumbs, and egg to meat. It is served on a plate with rice or bread, not in a bun."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The secret to a tender patty is cold fat and thorough mixing. Use your hands to mix the mince for at least 2 minutes until the mixture is smooth and slightly sticky. This develops the protein structure and stops the patty falling apart. Chill the shaped patties in the fridge for 15 minutes before cooking if you have time. This helps them hold their shape."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
